@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Enterprise Agreement & Terms of Service";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-10 bg-white p-5 rounded-4 shadow-sm border border-light">
            <h1 class="fw-bold mb-4 text-primary"><i class="fas fa-file-signature me-3"></i>EthioChain Enterprise Agreement</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-5 border-bottom pb-4">Effective Date: April 2026</p>

            <h4 class="fw-bold mt-4"><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-success me-2"></i> 1. Acceptance of Terms</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary lh-lg mb-4">By registering for an account on the EthioChain Supply Chain Management System, you agree to these Terms of Service. This platform facilitates B2B procurement, inventory management, and logistics synchronization across the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia.</p>

            <h4 class="fw-bold mt-4"><i class="fas fa-id-card text-success me-2"></i> 2. Digital Identity & Fayda Integration</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary lh-lg mb-4">All enterprise operators must verify their identity using the National Digital ID (Fayda) system. You agree that the phone number and demographic data retrieved from Fayda is strictly utilized for anti-fraud protocols, ensuring marketplace integrity for Ethiopian suppliers and retailers.</p>

            <h4 class="fw-bold mt-4"><i class="fas fa-file-invoice-dollar text-success me-2"></i> 3. Trading Compliance</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary lh-lg mb-4">Vendors and procurement agents are obligated to comply with Ethiopian tax regulations, including standard VAT obligations and TIN (Tax Identification Number) verification. All digital transactions executed via integrated partners (e.g., Chapa, Telebirr, or CBE Birr) are subject to Ethiopian financial laws and National Bank of Ethiopia (NBE) directives.</p>

            <h4 class="fw-bold mt-4"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale text-success me-2"></i> 4. Dispute Resolution</h4>
            <p class="text-secondary lh-lg mb-4">In the event of a logistics or payment dispute between a verified Supplier and Retailer on EthioChain, parties agree to first seek arbitration within the jurisdiction of the Addis Ababa Chamber of Commerce and Sectoral Associations before pursuing formal litigation under Ethiopian commercial law.</p>

            <hr class="my-5" />
            <p class="small text-muted text-center">© 2026 EthioChain SCM. For assistance, contact our Addis Ababa support center.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
